            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 01/05/2020 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, physical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with audible wheeze. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypercapnic respiratory failure. Oxygen saturation was monitored continuously via pulse oximetry. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Pulmonary rehabilitation advice and inhaler technique education were provided prior to discharge. He is discharged home in a stable condition and we recommend close follow-up and optimisation of his long-term COPD management. Please do not hesitate to contact us with any queries.</div>
               </text>
